728 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Create a Hub for Black Culture and Arts Due to a lack of resources for Black Americans, many have been forced to move out of the Santa Barbara area, taking their cultural traditions with them. Many who lived in Santa Barbara several decades ago have cited the notable decrease in African-American arts and social gathering places in modern-day Santa Barbara, recounting that several of their cultural hubs now feel gentrified. [13] This presents an opportunity for Healing Justice Santa Barbara to establish itself as a central cultural hub that preserves and uplifts Black arts, music, and traditions. By hosting cultural events, creating community spaces, and supporting Black artists, HJSB can both celebrate heritage and rebuild a sense of belonging for the Black community. Additionally, positioning itself as a cultural anchor would allow Healing Justice Santa Barbara to attract funding, strengthen partnerships, and expand its visibility as a leader in preserving and revitalizing Black culture.)
/E (Create a Hub for Black Culture and Arts Due to a lack of resources for Black Americans, many have been forced to move out of the Santa Barbara area, taking their cultural traditions with them. Many who lived in Santa Barbara several decades ago have cited the notable decrease in African-American arts and social gathering places in modern-day Santa Barbara, recounting that several of their cultural hubs now feel gentrified. [13] This presents an opportunity for Healing Justice Santa Barbara to establish itself as a central cultural hub that preserves and uplifts Black arts, music, and traditions. By hosting cultural events, creating community spaces, and supporting Black artists, HJSB can both celebrate heritage and rebuild a sense of belonging for the Black community. Additionally, positioning itself as a cultural anchor would allow Healing Justice Santa Barbara to attract funding, strengthen partnerships, and expand its visibility as a leader in preserving and revitalizing Black culture.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
