734 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Structural Barriers for Black-Led Organizations Beyond competition, systemic funding barriers continue to disadvantage Black-led groups. A 2025 survey showed that 74% of Black-led nonprofits are underfunded and unable to hire staff. [19] Many grassroots organizations also struggle to meet grant requirements or demonstrate long track records that funders often demand. [20] The relationship gap adds another hurdle, since funders frequently support organizations they already know, leaving newer Black-led groups behind. [21] Additionally, 64% of Black nonprofit leaders reported that a lack of new racial equity funding is a top barrier to advancing their missions. [22] Structural bias and weak funder outreach can prevent HJSB from securing grants, even when their goals match.)
/E (Structural Barriers for Black-Led Organizations Beyond competition, systemic funding barriers continue to disadvantage Black-led groups. A 2025 survey showed that 74% of Black-led nonprofits are underfunded and unable to hire staff. [19] Many grassroots organizations also struggle to meet grant requirements or demonstrate long track records that funders often demand. [20] The relationship gap adds another hurdle, since funders frequently support organizations they already know, leaving newer Black-led groups behind. [21] Additionally, 64% of Black nonprofit leaders reported that a lack of new racial equity funding is a top barrier to advancing their missions. [22] Structural bias and weak funder outreach can prevent HJSB from securing grants, even when their goals match.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
